msgid "Store object information can come in a few different variations."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/json/store-object-info.md:81
msgid ""
"Firstly, \"impure\" fields, which contain non-intrinsic information about "
"the store object, may or may not be included."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/json/store-object-info.md:83
msgid ""
"Second, binary cache stores have extra non-intrinsic infomation about the "
"store objects they contain."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/json/store-object-info.md:85
msgid ""
"Thirdly, [`nix path-info --json --closure-size`](../../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-path-info.html#opt-closure-size) can compute some extra information "
"about not just the single store object in question, but the store object and "
"its [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-closure)."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/json/store-object-info.md:87
msgid ""
"The impure and NAR fields are grouped into separate variants below. See "
"their descriptions for additional information. The closure fields however as "
"just included as optional fields, to avoid a combinatorial explosion of "
"variants."
msgstr ""

